cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SIGMAI: Secure GIS-AI Interface"
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Maciel
    given-names: Luan da Silva Cortes
    email: herpetomantiqueira@gmail.com
    alias: "MACIEL, L. S. C."
repository-code: "https://github.com/LuanCortesM/SIGMAI"
url: "https://plugins.qgis.org/plugins/sigmai/"
abstract: >-
  SIGMAI is a QGIS plugin that lets AI assistants operate QGIS through a local,
  token-protected command interface instead of screen automation. It exposes a
  standards-compliant Model Context Protocol server, a consent layer that keeps
  the user in control of every action that changes the project or writes a file,
  and a cartographic engine that composes page-aware map layouts and audits them
  against an explicit, machine-readable rulebook.
keywords:
  - QGIS
  - GIS
  - cartography
  - Model Context Protocol
  - artificial intelligence
  - reproducible research
  - map quality
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.2.2
